db/ref 1083 #uuid "d57288de-03b6-5e03-a4e2-8d3ffd50ab56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186349426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351077 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d4d8bd85-6ed0-50a7-beec-e978018f54bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351525 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186351077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351525 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351525 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351525 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}-12{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351525 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27104c42-2b8b-56dd-a6a7-0d4bf0700fca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351525 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}10 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}65 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{19}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}65 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-21 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369721 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369726 #edb/ref 175